From f6d086a133158a73e1af57cc348465b75845969e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:22:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-96: Alt+click goes a layer down each time;
 Ctrl(+Alt)+Space+click zooms, like Blend (0.96.0)

Blend (Artboard modifier keys): "Select an object underneath another object:
hold down Alt and click once for each layer of objects" and "Zoom in: hold
down Ctrl+Spacebar while clicking; zoom out: Ctrl+Alt+Spacebar". Here
Alt+click only took the innermost element, and there was no click zoom.
- altPick: every element under the point (the overlay out of the way), inside
  the form; the first Alt+click takes the top one (as before), each next one
  the one below the current selection, round again at the bottom; the click
  that follows the press no longer re-picks.
- Ctrl+Space held: ZSP, the hand's shield with a zoom-in cursor (zoom-out
  with Alt); a press zooms one step with the page point under the pointer kept
  there (zoomAt); Space up (or leaving the window) ends it.

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 160, smoke 186, panels, real VS Code 159):
probe (the form selected: Alt+click x4 = spbSave > Panel2 > @form > spbSave,
and spbSave > Panel1 > @form > spbSave on the other page; Ctrl+Space shows
the zoom-in shield, a click = 1.1, Space up hides it, Ctrl+Alt+Space + click
= 1; nothing selected or written).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
